"prose": [
{
"from": 194,
"to": 197,
"text": "The block runs: the formatter and the linter; each touched crate's units; the filtered new-case entries (each selects only this chunk's new cases: 0 on the untouched tree, read red-vacuous at baseline, as the last chunk's were); the integration binaries this chunk touches; the host read; the whole unit, integration and e2e layers through the harness; then the operator pass."
},
{
"from": 199,
"to": 206,
"text": "**What is not run, and why:** no round, no live entry, no live start, no rig start, no mutation run and no witness run (`inputs#I1`); no `cargo deny` entry (no dependency moves; CI's `supply-chain` runs it); no fuzz target (the lineage rule reads members of a line the bounded events reader already parsed, and every name it keeps passes `ViolaName::try_new`, which `fuzz/fuzz_targets/viola_name.rs` already covers — security S4 holds with no new parser surface). The start order changes (a boot-path touchpoint, `start_state`): the harness boot smoke runs in the operator pass, and `harness_lifecycle` runs in the block. Every test start runs under a test-owned home with `VIOLA_*` dropped and set only where a case declares it; every new wait is the existing bounded `wait_events` / `Wrapper::kill` wait, under the 20 s lint."
},
{
"from": 208,
"to": 212,
"text": "**Older binaries.** The pinned product of today (the release build of `f274938f`) drives this session and reads only its own home's instances; every test binary of this chunk writes only test-owned homes, so this session's product never meets a `lineage` line here. Where it could: an older `viola list` or wrapper run over a home a newer start wrote — it counts the line under `skipped.unknown_kinds` (the BAY line's skip counts) and reads everything else whole (architecture · decision/mixed-version-tolerance); no test of this chunk runs an older binary."
},
{
"from": 214,
"to": 216,
"text": "**The remove-the-guard controls** are implement's one-shot `gate.py control` runs, never entries, each fired on its own filtered entry, its case named, `--timeout 600`; each case fails on its own bounded assertion, so a `timeout` reading would NOT read the guard as held."
},
{
"from": 218,
"to": 222,
"text": "| id | File | The edit removes | Case | Entry | |---|---|---|---|---| | `last-wins` | `crates/viola-state/src/replay.rs` | the replace in `apply_lineage_line` (a held value kept: first line wins) | `lineage_rule_a_later_line_with_no_parent_clears_it` | `ctl-state` | | `name-check` | `crates/viola-state/src/board.rs` | the `ViolaName::try_new` filter on a link pair | `board_read_links_are_sorted_deduplicated_and_name_checked` | `ctl-state` | | `revive-keep` | `src/cmd/revive.rs` | the recorded lineage handed into `Launch` (a default in its place) | `revive_keeps_the_recorded_parent_and_role` | `ctl-revive` |"
},
{
"from": 224,
"to": 225,
"text": "`evidence/remove-the-guard.md`, which the controls criterion names, has no listed producer: step 23's close writes it with the Write tool from the controls' lines, a step outside the block."
}
],
